  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract activity in Colorado through FY2026 to date totals $13.3B in obligations across 21,122 awards, with an average award size of $630K. Obligations are down 17.3% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $7.2B, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $1.6B and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration at $1B. Major vendors include LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP at $2.3B and SIERRA NEVADA COMPANY, LLC at $2.1B. Aircraft Manufacturing and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences each account for $1.5B in obligations. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing accounts for $1.3B, and Engineering Services accounts for $925M. Year-to-date totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress. Historical context shows obligations peaked at $16.1B in FY25 and are currently at $13.3B for FY26 to date. Use these figures to size opportunities and to prioritize outreach to high-spend agencies and incumbents in aerospace, R&D, and defense-related services.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies drive federal contract spending in Colorado?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $7.2B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs follows with $1.6B, and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration follows with $1B. The Department of Energy, Department of Homeland Security, and General Services Administration also appear among the top buyers with $845M, $532M, and $474M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the key contractors and industries to watch in Colorado?",
        "body": "LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP and SIERRA NEVADA COMPANY, LLC are the top vendors, receiving $2.3B and $2.1B respectively. Aerospace-related industries dominate obligations: Aircraft Manufacturing and R&D in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences each have $1.5B, Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing has $1.3B, and Engineering Services has $925M. Pharmacy benefits, facilities support, and other professional services also register significant obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
